# YouTube Data API v3 Integration for Lux

This guide shows how to use the Lux YouTube integration added for issue #68.
It uses YouTube Data API v3 OAuth2 bearer tokens and follows Lux conventions:

- Lenses read YouTube resources.
- Prisms create/update/transition YouTube resources.
- Tests use `Req.Test`; no real Google credentials are required for unit tests.

## Configuration

YouTube write operations require OAuth2 scopes such as:

- `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/youtube.readonly` for read-only lenses
- `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/youtube` for uploads and metadata writes
- `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/youtube.force-ssl` for live chat messages

Set the access token in runtime config:

```bash
export YOUTUBE_ACCESS_TOKEN="ya29.example-oauth-access-token"
```

`config/runtime.exs` maps this to:

```elixir
config :lux, :api_keys,
  youtube: env!("YOUTUBE_ACCESS_TOKEN", :string!, required: false)
```

You can also set it directly in tests or local scripts:

```elixir
Application.put_env(:lux, :api_keys, youtube: "test-youtube-token")
```

## Read examples

Fetch video metadata:

```elixir
alias Lux.Lenses.YouTube.Videos.GetVideo

GetVideo.focus(%{id: "VIDEO_ID"})
```

List popular videos with pagination:

```elixir
alias Lux.Lenses.YouTube.Videos.ListVideos

ListVideos.focus(%{
  chart: "mostPopular",
  max_results: 10,
  page_token: "NEXT_PAGE_TOKEN"
})
```

Get live broadcast status:

```elixir
alias Lux.Lenses.YouTube.LiveBroadcasts.GetBroadcast

GetBroadcast.focus(%{id: "BROADCAST_ID"})
```

List upcoming broadcasts:

```elixir
alias Lux.Lenses.YouTube.LiveBroadcasts.ListBroadcasts

ListBroadcasts.focus(%{broadcast_status: "upcoming"})
```

Get stream health and CDN quality:

```elixir
alias Lux.Lenses.YouTube.LiveStreams.GetStreamHealth

GetStreamHealth.focus(%{id: "STREAM_ID"})
```

List live chat messages:

```elixir
alias Lux.Lenses.YouTube.LiveChat.ListMessages

ListMessages.focus(%{live_chat_id: "CHAT_ID", max_results: 50})
```

## Write examples

Create a scheduled live broadcast:

```elixir
alias Lux.Prisms.YouTube.LiveBroadcasts.InsertBroadcast

InsertBroadcast.handler(%{
  title: "Lux Demo Stream",
  scheduled_start_time: "2026-05-06T18:00:00Z",
  privacy_status: "private",
  enable_auto_start: false,
  enable_auto_stop: false
}, %{name: "Lux Agent"})
```

Create a live stream with quality controls:

```elixir
alias Lux.Prisms.YouTube.LiveStreams.InsertStream

InsertStream.handler(%{
  title: "Primary RTMP 1080p",
  ingestion_type: "rtmp",
  resolution: "1080p",
  frame_rate: "60fps"
}, %{name: "Lux Agent"})
```

Bind stream to broadcast:

```elixir
alias Lux.Prisms.YouTube.LiveBroadcasts.BindStream

BindStream.handler(%{id: "BROADCAST_ID", stream_id: "STREAM_ID"}, %{name: "Lux Agent"})
```

Transition broadcast lifecycle:

```elixir
alias Lux.Prisms.YouTube.LiveBroadcasts.TransitionBroadcast

TransitionBroadcast.handler(%{id: "BROADCAST_ID", broadcast_status: "testing"}, %{name: "Lux Agent"})
TransitionBroadcast.handler(%{id: "BROADCAST_ID", broadcast_status: "live"}, %{name: "Lux Agent"})
TransitionBroadcast.handler(%{id: "BROADCAST_ID", broadcast_status: "complete"}, %{name: "Lux Agent"})
```

Start a resumable upload session:

```elixir
alias Lux.Prisms.YouTube.Videos.InsertVideo

InsertVideo.handler(%{
  title: "Lux Upload Demo",
  description: "Uploaded through Lux",
  privacy_status: "private",
  mime_type: "video/mp4",
  content_length: 1_048_576
}, %{name: "Lux Agent"})
```

Send a live chat message:

```elixir
alias Lux.Prisms.YouTube.LiveChat.InsertMessage

InsertMessage.handler(%{live_chat_id: "CHAT_ID", text: "Hello from Lux"}, %{name: "Lux Agent"})
```

## Testing

Run the YouTube unit tests:

```bash
mix test.unit test/unit/lux/integrations/youtube/client_test.exs test/unit/lux/lenses/youtube test/unit/lux/prisms/youtube
```

The tests assert request method, path, query parameters, OAuth bearer header, JSON payloads,
error mapping, upload session handling, lifecycle transition validation, live chat payloads,
and stream quality validation.
